UID:37d5af355062cfe5@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair 
 and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHA
 NGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal 
 are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP
  for Bon Bons: Mother Ginger's Bon Bons — Costume (you provide): Pink 
 Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes
  *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup: Light Stag
 e Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Pink Ha
 t\; Prop (BA provides): Lollipop\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\
 n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applie
 d to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeli
 ner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be 
 sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage li
 ghts)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh
  tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•
   Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to
  delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event 
 of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\
 n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang cost
 umes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor 
 while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or la
 under any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while 
 in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on
  costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfu
 me or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assig
 ned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage wh
 ile in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove cost
 umes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Rem
 ove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their u
 se\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply
  fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\
 n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that 
 may damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
